# AC semantic probe: callee signature change (PLAN-796 T-06, executed)

status: executed — the CALLEE signature flip (plus the matching call
argument) changes the caller's called-sigs-fp key component
(contract-decision D7), so the old result is a miss and the fresh
recompute republishes under the new key. One key never holds two
contents.

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2"
  id: "ac.sema.callee-sig-change"
  tags: ["ac-semantics", "probe"]
  source: { file: "src/callee-sig.at", syntax: "auto", path: "callee-sig.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "callee-sig", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
      options: {
        recipe: "sema/query-v1",
        sema: { package: "probe", module: "callee-sig", kind: "infer-body", fn: "main" },
        steps: [
          { op: "query" },
          { op: "edit-source", from: "helper(a int, b int)", to: "helper(a bool, b int)" },
          { op: "edit-source", from: "helper(2, 3)", to: "helper(true, 3)" },
          { op: "query" }
        ]
      },
      expect: { completion: "success", probe: [
        { cache: "published", compute_calls: 1, stages_include: ["publish"] },
        { cache: "published", compute_calls: 1, stages_include: ["infer"] }
      ] } }
  ]
}
```
